\tag{fdip}
\title{Hamiltonians and quantum scalar fields}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The coupled quartic chain of \ref{fdip-00GV} transfers complete
spatial configurations through a positive kernel. Its
spectral transfer Hamiltonian from \ref{fdip-00GZ} depends on a nonzero
time step. What continuous-time Hamiltonian describes this
interaction, and how do its wavefunctions give quantum field
measurements and Euclidean correlations?}

\p{The potential remains continuous and coercive as in
[the slice construction](fdip-00GU). Closed quadratic forms and
the spectral theorem provide the operator framework;
\citet{Theorem 2.14, p. 81}{teschl2014quantum} and
\citet{Theorem 1.1, p. 2}{simon1999feynman} supply the form
representation and heat-kernel formula. Sobolev derivatives,
local elliptic regularity and Gaussian integration are used below.}

